      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sharpsburg was founded by James Sharp in 1826 who bought 257 acres and built a log cabin for his wife Isabella.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sharpsburg%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first factory was Heinz Noble & Company, later known as the Heinz Company, which began producing bricks in Sharpsburg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sharpsburg%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A covered bridge in Sharpsburg, photographed in black and white, is one of the few remaining historic structures in the borough.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
